---
description: Access HTTP tests are cannot-only; one guest test per controller action
alwaysApply: true
---

# Access integration tests

`test/integration/{resource}_access_integration_test.rb` covers cannot / no-access only: guest redirect, tenant 404, denied action. Authorized success and display stay in the resource integration file.

One guest test per controller action. Index and show are two entry points. Isolation and deny names omit `user`. Do not test currency formatting. Index isolation asserts unique foreign copied-text with `count: 0`. Titles shared across tenants do not prove exclusion.

Full testing rule: `minitest-rails.mdc`.

```ruby
# bad
test "alex on northwind sees acme corp" do
end

test "user cannot access a customer from another organization" do
end

test "guests are redirected to sign in" do
  get customers_path
end
```

```ruby
# good
# test/integration/customer_access_integration_test.rb
test "guests cannot access customers list page" do
  get customers_path
  assert_redirected_to new_session_path
end

test "guests cannot access a customer detail page" do
  get customer_path(customers(:acme_inc))
  assert_redirected_to new_session_path
end

test "cannot access a customer from another organization" do
  get customers_path
  assert_select "a", text: "Acme Inc", count: 0
  get customer_path(customers(:acme_inc))
  assert_response :not_found
end
```

Every authenticated HTML controller gets an access file once it has HTTP tests. Skip access when every action is public, or when the cannot case is already the resource action (`session` logout). Model `in_org` tests stay in `test/models/`.
